{
  "query": "Your team at Nimbus Arcade is building a real time multiplayer racing game that must update player profiles and leaderboards instantly as events occur. Peak usage reaches about 180,000 concurrent players in a single North America region and the app requires sub second reads and writes with real time listeners so clients stay in sync. You want a fully managed database that scales automatically and supports event driven updates to connected devices. Which Google Cloud database service should you choose?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Cloud Spanner with a regional instance",
      "explanation": "This service provides horizontally scalable relational storage with strong consistency in a single region",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Firestore in single region mode",
      "explanation": "This service supports real time subscriptions and automatically scales for document oriented workloads with low latency",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Bigtable with a single node cluster",
      "explanation": "This service is a wide column database optimized for high throughput workloads such as time series and operational analytics",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL with one high memory instance",
      "explanation": "This service offers managed relational databases with vertical scaling and optional read replicas",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    }
  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct choice is <b>Cloud Firestore in single region mode</b>.</p><p><b>Cloud Firestore in single region mode</b> is a fully managed, serverless document database that automatically scales to very high concurrency and provides sub second reads and writes. It natively supports real time listeners so connected clients receive event driven updates as data changes, which is exactly what a fast paced multiplayer game with live leaderboards requires. A single region deployment keeps latency low for players concentrated in one region and it also reduces cost compared to multi region while still meeting the need for instant updates.</p><p><i>Cloud Spanner with a regional instance</i> offers strong consistency and horizontal scale for relational workloads, yet it does not provide native real time client listeners. You would need to build a separate change notification and fan out layer to keep clients in sync, which adds complexity and cost for this use case.</p><p><i>Cloud Bigtable with a single node cluster</i> is not appropriate because a single node lacks high availability and is not recommended for production. Bigtable also does not provide native real time listeners to clients and is better suited for very large throughput key value and time series workloads rather than event driven sync to end user devices.</p><p><i>Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL with one high memory instance</i> cannot scale horizontally to handle large numbers of concurrent connections at sub second latency and it does not support real time listeners to push changes to clients. It would become a bottleneck under the stated concurrency.</p>",
